// probe: a_bare - is the bare name alone a declaration the engine takes.
//
// The `@` is gone from line 5. What run 36726960949 measured is that a `@`
// after a plugin type is a parse error with the column sitting on the `@`
// (c_handle.nvgt:5 (13), e2e_types.nvgt:14 (13)), and this file is that same
// line with the character removed - so its answer is the other half: whether
// a bare name declares at all, and whether the simple type next to it in
// b_decl behaves the same way.
//
// Nothing is called. The question is about the declaration and only that, so
// a failure here is the declaration and never a call going wrong.
#pragma plugin nvmidi

void main() {
	print("A1");
	midi_output out;
	print("A2");
	midi_output d;
	print("A3");
}
